, "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past & Past Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was or was not happening at a particular time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\">Affirmative</span> form: subject + was/were + verb-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\">Negative</span> form: subject + was/were + not + verb-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the words <span class =\"strong\">when</span>, <span class =\"strong\">while</span> and <span class =\"strong\">as</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I wasn't sleeping <span class =\"strong\">when</span> you called.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">While</span> I was reading a book, I heard a noise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">As</span> I was waiting at the airport, I listened to music. <br/> <br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talking About the Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense (<span class =\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future.<br /> You can also use the modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span> and <span class =\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is<span class =\"strong\"> 'll</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The modals <span class =\"strong\">might</span> and <span class =\"strong\">may</span> go before the verb. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They talk about future possibility or a chance that something will happen. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Might</span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%).", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "give a call", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to call someone using the telephone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll give him a call when I have some time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "weather forecast", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a description of what kind of weather is likely to happen in the future", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The weather forecast for today is rain.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "ice cream sandwich", "type": "name"}, {"content": "ice cream between two cookies", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We made ice cream sandwiches yesterday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " to stumble", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hit your foot on something when you are walking or running so that you fall or almost fall ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco stumbled into me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to fly off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move through the air quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The cookies went flying off into the air.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to land", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to come down through the air and hit the ground", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The plate landed on the floor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to cut", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to break the skin and make it bleed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The broken pieces cut his hand.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stitch", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece of thread used to sew the edges of a wound together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Marco might get a few stitches on his hand.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go on the Internet. Find an English radio station.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to it for 10 minutes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you listen, listen for the different tenses. Can you spot them all?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list. Write down the ones you hear.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare your list with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I can listen for actions in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can listen for events in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can talk about actions and events in the past and future.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le09ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Did you talk to Peter?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yeah, he was getting ready for exams when I talked to him.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: If I get a chance, I might give him a call. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  Where are you now?<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: I'm in the Congo. The flight to Cairo is delayed for 5 hours! What will I do?"}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob11re2img01.jpg", "time": "16400", "id": 2, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Why? <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: The weather forecast for today is rain, rain and more rain! Hey, you never told me about the rest of your evening with Marco.<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Oh right, so, we made ice cream sandwiches with the cookies Marco made. <br/>\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Right."}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob11re2img05.jpg", "time": "35000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: While I was taking them out of the fridge, Marco stumbled into me. Then, the sandwiches flew up into the air. The plate landed on the ground and broke. <br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Sally</span>: Wow!<br />\n<span class =\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: It gets better. Marco cut his hand on the broke